  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Order these fractions from smallest to largest.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\frac12,\\ \\frac16,\\ \\frac13,\\ \\frac1{10},\\ \\frac14$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac1{10},\\ \\frac16,\\ \\frac14,\\ \\frac13,\\ \\frac12$",
          "worked": "The numerators are all 1, so the larger the denominator, the smaller the fraction.\n\n$$\\frac1{10}<\\frac16<\\frac14<\\frac13<\\frac12$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\frac34,\\ \\frac38,\\ \\frac18,\\ \\frac14,\\ \\frac98$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac18,\\ \\frac14,\\ \\frac38,\\ \\frac34,\\ \\frac98$",
          "worked": "Write the fractions with denominator 8:\n\n$$\\frac34=\\frac68,\\qquad\\frac14=\\frac28.$$\n\nCompare the numerators:\n\n$$\\frac18<\\frac14<\\frac38<\\frac34<\\frac98.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\frac13,\\ \\frac49,\\ \\frac56,\\ \\frac36,\\ \\frac23$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac13,\\ \\frac49,\\ \\frac36,\\ \\frac23,\\ \\frac56$",
          "worked": "Use denominator 18:\n\n$$\\frac13=\\frac6{18},\\quad\\frac49=\\frac8{18},\\quad\\frac56=\\frac{15}{18},$$\n\n$$\\frac36=\\frac9{18},\\qquad\\frac23=\\frac{12}{18}.$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\\frac13<\\frac49<\\frac36<\\frac23<\\frac56.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac1{18},\\ \\frac{16}{17},\\ \\frac9{18},\\ \\frac{17}{19},\\ \\frac5{16}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac1{18},\\ \\frac5{16},\\ \\frac9{18},\\ \\frac{17}{19},\\ \\frac{16}{17}$\n\nCompare equivalent fractions using common denominators.",
          "worked": "Compare successive fractions using common denominators:\n\n$$\\frac1{18}=\\frac8{144}<\\frac{45}{144}=\\frac5{16}.$$\n\n$$\\frac5{16}<\\frac8{16}=\\frac12=\\frac9{18}.$$\n\n$$\\frac9{18}=\\frac12=\\frac{19}{38}<\\frac{34}{38}=\\frac{17}{19}.$$\n\n$$\\frac{17}{19}=\\frac{289}{323}<\\frac{304}{323}=\\frac{16}{17}.$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\\frac1{18}<\\frac5{16}<\\frac9{18}<\\frac{17}{19}<\\frac{16}{17}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\frac78,\\ \\frac45,\\ \\frac56,\\ \\frac34,\\ \\frac38$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac38,\\ \\frac34,\\ \\frac45,\\ \\frac56,\\ \\frac78$",
          "worked": "Use denominator 120:\n\n$$\\frac78=\\frac{105}{120},\\quad\\frac45=\\frac{96}{120},\\quad\\frac56=\\frac{100}{120},$$\n\n$$\\frac34=\\frac{90}{120},\\qquad\\frac38=\\frac{45}{120}.$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\\frac38<\\frac34<\\frac45<\\frac56<\\frac78.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$2\\frac14,\\ \\frac35,\\ 1\\frac3{10},\\ 2\\frac26,\\ 1\\frac15$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac35,\\ 1\\frac15,\\ 1\\frac3{10},\\ 2\\frac14,\\ 2\\frac26$",
          "worked": "First compare whole-number parts: $\\frac35<1<2$.\n\nFor the numbers between 1 and 2,\n\n$$1\\frac15=1\\frac2{10}<1\\frac3{10}.$$\n\nFor the numbers between 2 and 3,\n\n$$2\\frac14=2\\frac3{12}<2\\frac4{12}=2\\frac26.$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\\frac35<1\\frac15<1\\frac3{10}<2\\frac14<2\\frac26.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
